        "params": {
          "text": "## A report that lands on real paper\n\nOpen the **Quarterly Review** tab. It is ordinary markdown, plus two things\nthe flow provides:\n\n`![[Monthly Units]]` places what a node produced, by that node's **name** \u2014\nhere a chart and a table. `![[Monthly Units|width=60%]]` sizes it where it\nsits, which is the answer to \"my chart jumped to the next page\".\n\n**Page Setup\u2026** on the report toolbar owns the rest, and this page uses it:\na **cover** with a subtitle and date, **A4 portrait**, running **header and\nfooter** with `{page}` of `{pages}`, and numbering that starts after the\ncover.\n\nIn the body: a fenced ```columns block puts prose beside a chart, and\n`\\pagebreak` on a line of its own starts the detail on a fresh sheet.\n\n**Try it.** Press **F5** so the nodes produce something, then look at the\npreview \u2014 real sheets, with the margins and running heads where they will\nprint. **\u25a6** on the toolbar lays every page out at once. **Export PDF\u2026** and\n**Save HTML\u2026** both come off the same routines, so they agree.\n",
          "width": 460,
          "height": 440
        },
        "code": null,
        "label": null,
        "description": "",
